  "goodToKnow": "Der Ortsteil is a district or part of a municipality, often a formerly independent village that has been incorporated (eingemeindet) into a larger town or city. Many German municipal reforms in the 1970s merged small villages into larger Gemeinden, so addresses often read like Stadt X, Ortsteil Y. In big cities, people say Stadtteil or Viertel for the equivalent; Ortsteil sounds more rural or administrative."
